{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "system-prompt-build",
  "title": "How the shared system prompt is built",
  "description": "How agent-config builds `instructions/AGENTS.md`, the one global instruction file every coding agent reads.\n\n**Layout.** There are two rows. On top: Sources (left), Build (middle) and Agent files (right). Below: Prompt blocks (under Sources) and the Apply step (under Build). The six section files sit in a 2×3 grid. Their wires rise to one labelled line along the top of the board, which sections.toml joins, into the top of *Build: wrap and join*. The generators enter the build step from the left. The four block files feed the mcp-protocols generator through one labelled line. The seven agent links join one labelled teal line into AGENTS.md.\n\n- **Sources**: six section files in `instructions/sections/`. sections.toml sets order and groups. Principle files, harnesses.toml and task-routing.toml feed the principles and routing generators.\n- **Prompt blocks**: four core MCP servers' cli.ts print their blocks to mcp_protocols.py, which uses the machines list from mcp/servers.toml. `--write` writes block + sha256 to four block files, and those join in server-name order into the mcp-protocols generator. The red ends are a missing cli.ts and a drift found by --check.\n- **Build**: three generators feed the build step (merge glyph), which writes AGENTS.md. The size limits lead to *Build fails*.\n- **Apply step**: instructions/apply.py runs the build, backs up the stale copy, reads agents.toml, runs mcp_protocols.py --check, exits 1 while stale and creates or repairs the links. Root apply.py runs it after the MCP step. The Hub page edits section files, and every save rebuilds.\n- **Loop**: the orange \"edit through the link\" wire runs from Claude Code back to AGENTS.md. The loop note under the agent files explains it.\n\nColors: blue source, violet script or the runs it triggers, green generated, teal symlink, orange edits/Hub, red failure.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
